[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human HCT (ribonn)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=9,512): skew = 0.476, excess kurtosis = 0.677, D'Agostino K^2 p = 5.24e-94, Jarque-Bera p = 4.75e-118
  Normality of residuals: skew = 0.172, excess kurtosis = 0.531, D'Agostino K^2 p = 2.47e-26, Jarque-Bera p = 3.67e-35
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 294.725, p = 2.41e-32
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 59.495, p = 2.1e-26
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/ribonn/HCT/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_te_histogram_ribonn_HCT.png
